    "description": "Every barcode you've ever scanned started as a drawing in the sand.\nIn 1948 Norman Woodland drew Morse-code dots and dashes on a Florida beach and dragged them into narrow and wide lines. He and Bernard Silver patented it in 1952, and in 1974 a pack of Juicy Fruit gum became the first product scanned with a UPC, in Troy, Ohio, for 67 cents.",
